      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While small amounts are unlikely to cause a severe reaction, it's still recommended to exercise caution and consult with your doctor or pharmacist about safe consumption levels. Even minimal amounts of tyramine-rich foods like cheese or soy sauce can add up and potentially interact with your MAOI medication. Given your concerns about protein intake, consider focusing on protein-rich, non-tyramine foods like chicken, fish, beans, and lentils, and talk to your doctor about potential alternative sources of protein.",
      "source": "target",
